WEBVTT

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.990
Six years earlier
Near the Camellian border

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:31.060
Hold fast! We are proud Camellian warriors!

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.940
Dayereh is nothing to fear!

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.060
Rugis!

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.480
Sorry to keep you, Rugis!

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.230
Leon! Fernando!

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.520
We'll drive them off in a single push!

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.520
The Dominion of Olivier.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:38.480
One of the two great principalities that have
served the Kingdom of Hortensia.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:42.800
"Previous Archduke of Olivier,
Former Royal Order Commander"
 "Leon D. Olivier"

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.940
It has flourished under its wise leader, Leon D. Olivier,

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:47.190
but during Rugis's uprising,
Duke Leon followed the king to his death.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.850
Adelheid, his adopted daughter and heiress,

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.560
was to have succeeded him in his position,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.480
but due to strenuous objection by
an orthodox faction of the nobility,

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.850
the Dominion of Olivier was stripped of its title

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:02.730
and annexed into the kingdom
as one of its territories.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.250
August, 771, New Holy Era

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.060
Assassins from Dayereh...

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:16.560
A crimson dragon... There is no depth
to which this man Rugis will not sink.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.900
It is unlikely that a war with
Camellia can be avoided.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.400
However,

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.900
we have yet to fully come together.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.150
You mean Olivier.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.940
We cannot allow anyone who would
harbor a witch to go unchecked.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.330
Kingdom of Hortensia, Olivier

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.940
Wow, those look so yummy <i>moru</i> !

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.940
Olivier is a land that faces the sea, and all.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.560
The waters are inseparably linked
with the people's livelihoods.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.350
Wow, Marius, you know so much <i>moru</i> !

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:02.900
We're not here to see the sights, you two.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.350
Y-Yeah, we know.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.150
I have to ask, though,

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:11.190
couldn't the captain have sent one of his
own messengers to deliver this letter?

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.350
Oh, don't be like that.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:17.310
Georg is in a precarious position
and isn't at liberty to do anything.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:23.150
There are currently two great
factions in the Orthodox Church.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.020
Those of us who are moderates,

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.100
who follow the original teachings
of the Hortensian Orthodox Church,

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.100
and a radical faction, centered around Sir Didier.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:35.150
They impose heavy taxes on the people
under the pretext of strengthening the nation,

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.600
and behave as autocratically as possible.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.650
Then the Ecclesiastical Knights who
attacked us at Petale Village were...

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.310
Very likely.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:45.900
Now that the pope has promoted Sir Didier,

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:49.100
and the tide is turning against the moderates,

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.060
I would prefer that we have
some more trustworthy allies.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:57.690
Olivier is a dominion with plenty
of influence within the kingdom.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.440
I'm sure he wants to have them
on their side, whatever it takes.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:05.650
Aw, for heaven's sake,
and we have to travel all this way for that?

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:08.900
If there were blindingly beautiful
women or treasures waiting for us,

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.440
that would be another story...

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:13.770
Ah, Commander Adelheid,
the woman we're about to meet,

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:15.100
is an outstanding woman.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.650
What?! Why didn't you say so sooner?!

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:22.480
Is she pretty? Or more cute?
I prefer ladies who are pretty, myself.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:23.980
--You're the worst.
--You're the worst <i>moru</i> .

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.350
She's said to be the greatest
spear handler in the kingdom.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.770
That bit of information means nothing to me.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.980
Look, just tell me. Slender women aren't bad,

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.930
Adelheid...

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.900
but I like them when they have
curves in all the right places.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:33.230
Do you think she's okay?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.900
Qoo will stay hidden again <i>moru</i> .

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:38.440
Oh, I hope she's not all muscle,
since she's a Templar knight...

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.850
Sorry.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:47.740
"Hortensian Royal Order, 
Commander, Knights Templar"
"Adelheid Olivier"

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.230
Thank you for coming, Alfred.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:48.100
I thought this day might never arrive.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.480
I am honored that you remember me.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:51.600
You as well, Maurice.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.690
Yeah. I see you haven't changed much.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:58.560
This is my squire, Marius Casterede.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:59.120
You mean--

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.600
And me?

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.100
My name is Deflotte Danois.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:06.690
I am currently a page in the service of Alfred,

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:10.230
but in time, I will be a knight,
at which time it is my intent

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:14.940
to devote myself to the kingdom--
No, to <i>you</i> !

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:21.350
I-I am most pleased that there are those like yourself
who think so much of the kingdom.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:22.440
Oh, no.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:27.270
More than the kingdom,
I mean to serve the lovely Lady Adelheid--

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.730
That's enough of that.

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:31.600
What's the big idea, old man?
I was just getting to the good part.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.350
How do you figure that? I mean, honestly...

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:36.020
You saw what was happening!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.940
I see.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:43.520
Captain Georg is indeed one of
the few men with credibility,

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.980
even among the Ecclesiastical Knights.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:49.850
I would like to be of assistance to him.

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:51.230
Then we can tell the captain--

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:54.940
However, I need you to wait
a little longer for my response.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.730
Is something the matter?

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.350
For the last few days,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.100
we've had multiple reports
of suspicious ship and spy activity

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:05.020
at the mouth of the Torrent River
in southeast Olivier.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.690
Despite our security in the area
being strengthened,

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.850
we cannot afford to be careless.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:13.150
As such, I cannot act until
the situation dies down.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.690
That is what I want you to tell the captain.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:21.100
And after we came all the way here, too.
What a shame <i>moru</i> .

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:25.980
It was worth it for me to come,
just to get a look at Adelheid.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.020
Ooh... Well,

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:33.650
now that our errand is over,
I think I'll go down a cold ale!

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.770
Honestly, what a buffoon.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:43.480
Still, why did Adelheid want Alfred
to stay behind by himself?

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:49.060
They both lost their fathers
during Rugis's uprising.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:51.350
They probably have some catching up to do.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:58.900
I'm sorry I can't be more help.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:03.810
Not at all. If I were in your shoes,
I think I would have said the same.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:11.520
I have to keep Olivier safe, no matter what the cost.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.900
This is the land that my father loved.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:18.560
Duke Leon was a wonderful knight.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.730
I was hoping to catch up to my
great father as quickly as I could.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.350
You still have much to learn, Adelheid.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:33.520
You won't beat me this time!

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.770
That's the spirit. However,

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.400
you aren't closing in enough.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:39.730
Huh?

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:42.100
If you rely on the reach of your spear,

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.190
your chance of victory will
fall short of the spearhead.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:53.150
The tide of battle, like the tides
of Olivier's sea, are always changing.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:57.480
You must be able to anticipate it,
and charge in when victory presents itself.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.850
If you are unable to do that,

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.480
then you will never beat me as long as you live.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.230
However,

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.400
I've lost that chance forever.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:13.650
My father gave everything he had,
right up to the end,

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.230
trying to help the Camellians,
who were exhausted...

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:19.440
after fighting Dayereh.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:23.980
However, Rugis trampled on my father's memory,

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.270
and drew his bow against the kingdom.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.650
Welcome to--

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.150
--Come with us!
--Huh? Wait, let go of me!

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:33.770
--Hey!
--What is this?!

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.730
Those are Ecclesiastical Knights.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.150
What are they doing in this land?

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:39.520
They wouldn't!

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:40.900
--Come on, now!
--No, don't!

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.100
--Let go of my daughter!
--N-No!

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.480
Maurice, what is this?

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.810
A witch hunt.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:47.730
Impossible!

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.230
There's no way those women could be witches!

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.480
No, of course not.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:56.480
The witch hunt is merely an excuse.
It's likely they're after...

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:58.730
That's far enough.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.350
Hmm? There you are.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.150
For what reason is the
Ecclesiastical Order in my dominion,

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:06.190
committing these acts of tyranny?

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:07.440
Oh, no <i>moru</i> !

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:13.190
Adelheid Olivier, I understand
that you continue to search

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:16.230
for the missing Princess Mariel.

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:17.940
Adelheid...

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:19.600
Of course I am.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:22.350
As long as there is a chance she still lives,

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.940
it is our responsibility to keep searching for her.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:27.520
And then...

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.810
if you find the presumably dead princess,

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:35.730
you plan to make her an accomplice
to your schemes, is that the idea?

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.190
Sir Didier...

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:39.730
What is the meaning of this, Didier?

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:43.730
You are suspected of instigating a rebellion.

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:46.730
Of propping up a witch
impersonating the princess,

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:50.690
and plotting to overthrow the kingdom.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:52.940
That's a ridiculous falsehood.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.940
They've recognized that Adelheid
will side with the moderates,

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.900
and are here to eliminate her.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.770
Take the witches away!

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:02.520
Treat anyone who defies you as traitors to the kingdom

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.900
and punish them severely!

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:08.400
Marius, if you step forward, you'll be
giving them exactly what they want.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:09.650
Restrain yourself.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.900
I don't know what you think you're doing,

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.650
but I'll kick the ass of anyone
who raises their hand to a lady!

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.440
And I will be especially hard
on Ecclesiastical Knights!

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.020
That idiot!

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:23.440
Marius!

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:26.940
I can't stand by and watch this happen, either!

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.810
You simple fools!

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.810
Alfred, we have to save them!

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:37.020
Lord Albert...

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:43.440
You know full well what it would mean
to draw your sword, don't you?

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.810
What's the matter, Alfred?!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.730
Take me away.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:57.690
Just promise me that you
will not lay a hand on my people.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:01.730
I was always the one you were after, was I not?

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:04.560
Hmph, you have my word.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.230
Oh, no...

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:12.270
Adelheid...

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.060
Alfred...

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:21.770
If I were in your shoes, I would have
done the same. Pay no mind.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.270
Wh-What is that?!

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:35.400
The salamandre.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.730
Has Camellia launched an attack?

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:44.560
I bring a report!

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.480
Camellian forces have landed
at the mouth of the Torrent River!

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:51.100
You heard him, Didier.
If you're going to arrest me,

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.900
do it after we've driven them off!

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:57.190
Don't be absurd!
You're planning to escape in all the confusion!

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:59.270
Now is the time to defend the kingdom!

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:02.690
If Olivier falls to them,
Camellia will gain further momentum,

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:04.520
and will advance on the capital!

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:11.100
Very well. The Ecclesiastical Order
will lend you our aid.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.020
Adelheid...

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.940
Can we ask for your assistance?

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.730
That was always my intention.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:26.310
Alert all our forces!
Head for the Torrent River at once!

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:27.440
Ma'am!

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:32.730
What exactly is your goal here...

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:34.400
...Duke Rugis?

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.900
They're pressing us pretty hard!

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.810
We have to come up with some way out of this!

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.020
Thrusting through our enemy's chest

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:03.060
and claiming their leader's head
might be all we can do!

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.900
What kind of nonsense is that?!

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:08.810
He may be right.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:13.230
Fighting at the vanguard
is the way of Camellian leaders.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:16.770
I guarantee their general
is somewhere on the front line.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:24.650
I should have known you'd be
the one in command, Roy Bachelot!

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:28.520
You might at least offer me a smile.

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:34.270
Here we are, reunited, after once serving
side by side as Templar knights.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.730
Where is Rugis?!

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:40.480
I see you haven't changed at all.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.690
How dare you do this to my father...

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:50.900
Where is Rugis?!

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:56.060
Adelheid, I do not wish to fight you.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:15:00.270
Do you realize what you've done, Roy?!

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:04.350
You have absolutely no idea
what the reality of this nation is.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:09.980
Silence! I will choke the life out of you
in my father's place, right now!

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:16.560
Don't get in over your head.
Those are more than just scratches

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:19.020
you sustained while fighting those monsters.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.230
Damn...

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.440
Today is the day that I beat you

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.400
and succeed in slaying Rugis!

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.810
You're going to kill Rugis?

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.020
Then I suppose I'll have to accept your challenge.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:37.230
First you attack the capital,
now you plan to burn down Olivier?!

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:39.060
If Rugis orders it.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:43.190
Rugis betrayed the country and his friends,
and you still blindly follow him?!

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:45.520
What do you know of that great man?!

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.190
Ho...

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:50.650
Alfred...

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.650
We fight with you!

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:58.520
Sir Fernando's son.
I didn't know you were still alive.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:02.900
By losing to you, I realized how weak I was.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.350
I swore to my father that I would get stronger...

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:07.480
...to protect those who were dear to me!

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:12.520
Stand back! I will deal with him personally!

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:15.100
Remember, you are the lord of Olivier!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:18.230
If you were to fall in battle here,

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:21.480
who would protect Olivier,
the land that Duke Leon left behind?

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:29.770
I can't believe I let myself succumb to my grievances

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:31.730
and lose sight of our cause.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:37.900
Both of you, give me a hand with this.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:41.060
We're going to bring him down
and win this battle!

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.060
Right!

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:49.600
It must be time.

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:51.270
Retreat!

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:52.560
We're falling back!

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:53.560
Hurry!

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:57.270
Wh-What's happening?

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:00.100
Hold it!

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:01.270
Are you trying to escape?!

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:02.520
Why are you running?!

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:06.650
If you had kept on fighting,
you would have taken control of Olivier!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.850
To protect you.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:14.900
What does that mean? We are on opposite sides!

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:18.940
Heh, you never change, Adelheid.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:23.520
Always so straightforward... so noble.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:36.600
You will now accompany us
to the capital, as promised.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:39.190
Are you folks still here?!

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:41.100
Adelheid...

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:45.060
It is all right. Doing this will keep Olivier safe.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.190
Isn't there anything you can do, Alfred?

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.650
To protect you.

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.310
Just a moment, Sir Didier!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:03.850
Is there something more?

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:09.440
Yes. Thanks to Commander Adelheid's
efforts during this battle,

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:12.020
we managed to repel the Camellian forces.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:15.520
However, that is only a temporary outcome.

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:19.400
Their attacks are likely to continue.
And when they do,

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:23.770
it will prove much too dangerous
to have the commander out of this land.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:28.100
If Olivier is taken from us, it could
potentially pose a risk to the capital.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:31.940
Tell me, as the Ecclesiastical Order
charged with protecting the kingdom,

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:36.980
how do you plan on motivating
these forces without Adelheid?

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:39.770
Her arrest is not open for discussion!

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.560
It cannot be overturned for any reason!

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:43.940
Release her.

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:45.940
Huh?

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:49.850
There is indeed some logic in what you say.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.730
By driving back the Camellian forces,

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:56.150
I have seen for myself
her loyalty to the kingdom.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:59.150
We will hold off on taking her in for now.

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:02.900
Thank you very much.

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:07.940
However, this does not mean that
she is completely cleared of suspicion.

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:09.770
In time, we shall return.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:15.480
Gah, rotten jerk.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.810
We're out of the woods for now.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:19.980
Yeah.

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:27.230
Alfred isn't around <i>moru</i> .

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:29.980
Where could he have gone?

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:30.980
Qoo!

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:36.310
Oh, he's with Adelheid <i>moru</i> .

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:40.850
I don't know how to thank you.

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:43.230
I only did what needed to be done.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:46.270
If you are ever in trouble,
you may turn to Olivier.

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:48.440
We will welcome you gladly at any time.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.480
Adelheid...

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:59.520
The enemy that we--
I mean, that the whole kingdom is fighting--

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.020
who is it, exactly?

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:04.900
Alfred...

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:08.480
Why is the Orthodox Church depriving
the people of their peaceful lives

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:13.600
and suspecting you of rebelling against
them for searching for the princess?

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:17.900
When I take up this sword,
which my father left me,

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:20.230
what is it that I must fight?

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:30.940
Theresia...

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.230
What of Adelheid?

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:36.190
I cannot tell, exactly. However, I am sure...

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:40.020
So you can't see, even with your precognition?

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:44.850
I do not entirely understand my powers myself.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:50.600
I must say, though, Rugis sure did
come up with a wild plan.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:54.810
Ho, Adelheid is going to be thrown in prison?

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:59.060
As it stands, that is how the future will unfold.

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:02.350
Lead our soldiers on an invasion of Olivier.

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:03.310
At once, sir.

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:06.650
Wh-Why are you attacking Olivier?

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:12.310
By successfully defending her land,
Adelheid will prove her value,

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:15.650
and the Orthodox Church will no longer
be able to blindly move against her.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:18.810
Then you mean, it is to protect Adelheid?

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:20.730
Do not get the wrong idea, Theresia.

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:21.900
Huh?

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:26.020
Adelheid stands opposed to the pope.

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:32.060
Having the kingdom split into
two factions is more favorable for us.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:35.100
That's all there is to it.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:38.100
I wonder if he really meant that.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:42.350
There is no discerning what is in his mind.

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:47.310
Even so, the reason why I believe in Rugis...

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:51.400
...is because he is a knight among knights,
who at all times,

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:57.690
endeavors to fight for his people,
his friends, and those whom he loves.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.090
Chapter 5

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.090
Impact

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.090
~The Protected One~

00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:35.060
I will go fulfill my duty to lead the people.

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:37.400
As you wish, Princess Mariel.

00:23:37.400 --> 00:23:38.600
We didn't come here for the fun of it.

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:40.270
I do want to be free...

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:41.440
I'm going to keep the princess safe!

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:43.730
I'm putting a stop to this this instant!

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:46.940
See you later, everyone!

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:47.070
Chapter 6

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:47.070
True or False

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:47.070
~The Burden of a Princess~
